func readResp(t *testing.T, c net.Conn) string  // one line without the \n
```

To verify that Serve returns nil on cancel: run it in a goroutine, err := <-ch; expect nil.

Also confirm the listener is closed: after Serve returns, l.Accept() returns an error (or check via dial failure). Actually, once the listener is closed, new dials should fail. We can assert that a dial after cancel fails.

